      },
      "message": "fix(app): measure the cross drill about the work offset's spindle\n\nThe radial kernel measured every standoff (bar radius, station side,\nhop/clearance radii, the station-change chord law) about world Z through\nworld (0, 0), while the posts program about world Z through the work\noffset's origin. A bar moved off the world origin with G54 moved onto\nit drilled a different chain from G54 than the same bar on the origin\n(hop 26.444/32.444/46.444 mm vs 21.213, final clearance 35.770 vs 15).\n\n- operation/cross_spindle.rs: shift the holes into the spindle frame by\n  the wcs_context origin (collected once as GenJob::wcs_origin), measure\n  stock_r about that line, run the kernel, shift the chain back. An\n  origin on world Z runs the kernel untouched (on-origin bits unchanged).\n- spindle_law::turns also covers a mill-turn's cross drill, so a revolved\n  bar off its work offset is refused by name there too.\n- A plain lathe's cross drill refuses by name a part the axis fit cannot\n  read as turned (the mill-turn keeps drilling prismatic bars).\n\nFixes #67\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
