      "message": "fix(app): refuse a cross hole plunging away from the spindle\n\nReview fixes on PR #78:\n\n- A cross hole whose plunge points away from the spindle line (the\n  mouth's radial offset from world Z through the work offset, dotted\n  with the plunge, is positive) is refused by name in world\n  coordinates. The station law stood the tool on the mouth's side at\n  the hop radius - beyond the far face of a mill-turn block sitting off\n  G54 - and the rapid in to the mouth crossed the material.\n- On the shifted path a kernel refusal names the hole's world mouth,\n  not its spindle-frame point.\n- A lathe part whose axis fit returns a degenerate direction says so,\n  instead of \"its axis lies near the table\".\n- Tests: the away-plunge refusal (and the toward-plunge hole on the same\n  block still drilling), the world-coordinate kernel refusal, and\n  moving G54 under a generated mill-turn cross drill staling it with the\n  post refusing.\n\nRefs #67\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
